{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NN7GHGAoJQqGu63EXsNmLH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Soften Claim 1 scope: 'retrieval-gated equalizer effect' centered on LAMBADA with ARC-E as supporting evidence.\n  Dose-response framing still works but is acknowledged as preliminary (low-n benchmarks).\n  Claim 3 shifts wording to 'architecture-specific effect whose mechanism is opaque to standard and intermediate features' —\n  negative characterization results reported as informative (rules out trivial explanations), not as failure.\n  Claim 2 stays as binary contrast but adds explicit limitation paragraph about training token confound.\n  Attention visualization goes in as qualitative illustration, not quantitative evidence.\n  Paper positions itself as 'first to quantify and decompose the equalizer phenomenon' — phenomenon discovery paper, not mechanism paper.\n  Target EMNLP Findings; reviewers who value careful empirical work may push to Main.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Re-run lm-eval with --log_samples on 1.3B models (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2 at h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1)\n      for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge. Also collect 340M RetNet+HGRN2 (10 models) and 1.3B GDN\n      h3-1/h6-1/h24-1 missing configs. Compute per-example helped/hurt sets, pairwise Jaccard, and\n      per-example convergence metrics analogous to LAMBADA analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: false\n      hellaswag_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.18\n      hellaswag_jaccard_interpretation: \"near-random overlap, no systematic pattern\"\n      hellaswag_helped_hurt_net_direction: \"inconsistent across architectures and attention ratios\"\n      arc_easy_per_example_convergence: \"noisy/suggestive\"\n      arc_easy_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.12\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_pct: 38\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_p: 0.14\n      arc_easy_helped_hurt_asymmetry: \"present but unstable across attention ratios\"\n      arc_challenge_per_example_convergence: false\n      arc_challenge_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.15\n      arc_challenge_std_reduction_pct: 12\n      dose_response_rho_6benchmarks: -0.66\n      dose_response_rho_p: 0.16\n      n_benchmarks_per_example_confirmed_converging: 1\n      n_benchmarks_suggestive: 1\n      n_benchmarks_confirmed_non_converging: 4\n      gpu_hours_used: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 median 档下，equalizer effect 本质上是 retrieval-gated 的。LAMBADA 是纯粹的 last-word retrieval 任务，\n      attention 机制对此类任务有直接的结构性优势（回看上下文定位 target word），因此 per-example 收敛清晰。\n      ARC-Easy 包含部分 retrieval 成分（从选项中匹配已知事实），但混合了推理成分，导致 per-example 层面噪声大——\n      Jaccard 结构模糊，helped/hurt 集合随 attention ratio 变化不稳定，aggregate std 降低存在但不显著。\n      HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 主要依赖 commonsense reasoning 和 multi-step inference，attention 的贡献\n      分散在多种推理路径上而非集中在 retrieval 上，因此 per-example 分析确认了 aggregate 层面的非收敛：\n      不同架构被 attention 帮助/伤害的样本几乎是随机的，无系统性结构。\n      这使 dose-response 本质上变成了 2-point gradient：LAMBADA 强，ARC-E suggestive，其余 flat。\n      6 个 benchmark 的 Spearman ρ≈-0.66（在 [-0.75, -0.55] 范围内）但因 n=6 且非线性分布，p≈0.16 不显著——\n      这足以支持 \"retrieval demand 调节收敛强度\" 的叙事，但必须承认是 preliminary observation 而非 established relationship。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Retrieval Demand\", \"Aggregate ρ (std vs attn)\", \"Aggregate p\", \"Per-example Jaccard (mean pairwise)\", \"Std Reduction %\", \"Per-example Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"High\", -1.0, 0.008, 0.08, \"79%\", \"Converging (architecture-specific mechanism)\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Medium\", -0.7, 0.117, 0.12, \"38%\", \"Noisy/suggestive\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Low-Medium\", -0.3, 0.624, 0.15, \"12%\", \"Non-converging\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Low\", 0.3, 0.742, 0.18, \"-5%\", \"Non-converging (confirmed per-example)\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Low*\", 0.1, 0.608, \"N/A†\", \"3%\", \"Non-converging\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"Mixed\", -0.7, 0.117, \"N/A†\", \"22%\", \"Unclear (aggregate suggestive, no per-example data)\"]\n        notes: \"†Per-example data not collected for WinoGrande/MMLU in this experiment. *WinoGrande has coreference retrieval component; acknowledged in text.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Dose-response scatter plot — x-axis = retrieval demand (continuous, based on published task taxonomies), y-axis = convergence strength (Spearman ρ of cross-arch std vs attention ratio). LAMBADA clearly anchors the high-retrieval end (ρ=-1.0), ARC-E in the middle (ρ=-0.7), remainder clustered near zero. Fitted line shows negative trend but wide CI band due to n=6.\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-example Jaccard heatmaps for ARC-Easy (3×3 arch pairs, 5 attention ratios) — compared to LAMBADA equivalent. ARC-E shows no clear block structure; values fluctuate 0.05–0.20 without the consistent <0.10 pattern seen in LAMBADA. Visual contrast highlights LAMBADA's unique structure.\"\n      - \"Fig: HellaSwag helped/hurt sample identity stability — scatter showing helped/hurt sets at h3-1 vs h12-1 for each architecture. Near-random reassignment (points scattered around diagonal), confirming no systematic per-example effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002 的 median 结果确认 task-specificity 是真实的，但把 \"dose-response\" 的统计力量限制在了\n      descriptive level。论文的关键修辞策略：不要声称 dose-response 是 \"established\"，而是用\n      \"consistent with a retrieval-demand gradient\" + \"preliminary due to limited benchmark-level n\" 的措辞。\n      HellaSwag per-example 确认非收敛这一点很有价值——把 aggregate p=0.742 升级为 \"per-example confirmed\n      non-converging\"，排除了 \"aggregate 不显著只是因为 power 不够\" 的可能性。\n      ARC-E 的 noisy 结果实际上对叙事有利：它不是 retrieval 纯任务，所以 partial/noisy convergence\n      正好符合 \"retrieval demand 越高收敛越强\" 的 gradient story。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization Phase 2 (perplexity + topic/domain)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      在 Phase 1 surface features 全部 non-significant 的基础上，Phase 2 测试更深层特征：\n      (a) 各架构 pure recurrent baseline (h0) 下每个 LAMBADA 样本的 perplexity，\n      (b) 基于 LAMBADA 文本内容的 topic/domain 分布 (LDA 或预训练 topic model)。\n      检验 helped/hurt 样本是否在这些特征上可区分。\n    expected_results:\n      perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.031\n      perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.19\n      perplexity_gdn_direction: \"hurt samples have higher baseline perplexity (harder under pure recurrence)\"\n      perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.22\n      perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.08\n      perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.09\n      perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.13\n      topic_gdn_chi2_p: 0.34\n      topic_hgrn2_chi2_p: 0.51\n      topic_retnet_chi2_p: 0.28\n      cross_arch_perplexity_interaction_p: 0.07\n      n_features_significant_any_arch: 1\n      n_features_significant_cross_arch: 0\n      overall_mechanism_status: \"opaque to tested features; perplexity suggestive for GDN only\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档的核心假设是 mechanism 保持 opaque。Phase 2 的 perplexity 特征比 surface features 更有信息量，\n      因为它直接衡量 \"pure recurrence 下的困难度\"——直觉上，attention 最可能帮助那些 recurrence 本身处理不好的样本。\n      但这个直觉只在一个架构 (GDN) 上得到 marginal 验证 (p=0.031, d=0.19)：GDN 的 gated delta rule 机制\n      在高 perplexity 样本上可能有特定的弱点（例如需要精确的长距离 copy 但 delta rule 的 memory update\n      不够精确），attention 填补了这个缺口。HGRN2 和 RetNet 的 hierarchical/exponential decay 机制\n      处理困难样本的方式不同，perplexity 不是它们的瓶颈维度，所以信号消失。\n      Topic/domain 特征完全 non-significant：attention 的效果不是 \"对某些 domain 更有用\"，\n      而是在每个 domain 内部都有 architecture-specific 的帮助/伤害模式。\n      这实际上强化了 \"opaque mechanism\" 的叙事——连中间层特征 (perplexity) 也只给出了微弱线索，\n      说明 equalizer effect 的机制深嵌在 recurrence-attention 交互的计算层面。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Phase 2 feature analysis — helped vs hurt sample characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Architecture\", \"Test\", \"p-value\", \"Effect Size (d/V)\", \"Direction\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"GDN\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.031, \"d=0.19\", \"Hurt > Helped\", \"Marginal*\"]\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"HGRN2\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.22, \"d=0.08\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"RetNet\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.09, \"d=0.13\", \"Hurt > Helped (trend)\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"GDN\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.34, \"V=0.06\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"HGRN2\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.51, \"V=0.04\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"RetNet\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.28, \"V=0.07\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Perplexity × Arch interaction\", \"All\", \"Two-way ANOVA\", 0.07, \"η²=0.003\", \"—\", \"No (trend)\"]\n        notes: \"*Marginal: 0.01 < p < 0.05, below preregistered p<0.01 threshold for individual tests. After Bonferroni correction (6 tests), adjusted p=0.186.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Violin plots of baseline perplexity (h0) for helped vs hurt samples, one panel per architecture. GDN shows slight rightward shift for hurt samples; HGRN2 and RetNet distributions largely overlap. Annotated with p-values and effect sizes.\"\n      - \"Fig: Topic distribution bar charts for helped vs hurt, per architecture. Near-identical distributions — visual confirmation of non-significance.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 的 GDN perplexity signal (p=0.031) 在论文中的定位需要谨慎：它通过了 nominal 0.05 但\n      未通过 preregistered 0.01，且 Bonferroni 校正后不显著。论文应报告为 \"suggestive lead for future work\"，\n      不作为 claimed finding。关键叙事价值在负面结果的累积：surface features (Phase 1) + perplexity + topic\n      全部失败或 marginal，系统性地排除了从简单到中等复杂度的解释，让 \"mechanism is opaque\" 不是一句空话\n      而是有实证支撑的 negative characterization。这对 EMNLP Findings 审稿人来说是可接受的——\n      他们会 appreciate careful negative results over overclaimed positive ones。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns (1.3B)。\n      在 LAMBADA 样本上计算：(a) attention 聚焦位置分布，(b) attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 身份的相关性，\n      (c) 跨架构 attention pattern 相似度。\n    expected_results:\n      gdn_attention_entropy_mean: 3.2\n      hgrn2_attention_entropy_mean: 2.8\n      retnet_attention_entropy_mean: 3.0\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_gdn: 0.42\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_hgrn2: 0.58\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_retnet: 0.47\n      cross_arch_attention_cosine_similarity_mean: 0.35\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_gdn: 0.18\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_hgrn2: 0.27\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_retnet: 0.22\n      attention_pattern_correlation_mean: 0.22\n      passes_preregistered_threshold: false\n      qualitative_patterns_visible: true\n      gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档预测 attention correlation r=0.15–0.30，低于 preregistered r>0.3 threshold。\n      原因在于 attention 的作用路径是间接的：attention layer 不仅直接影响输出 logits，\n      还通过修改 hidden state 影响后续 recurrent layers 的计算。因此 attention weight pattern\n      本身只捕获了 \"attention 在看什么\" 而非 \"attention 如何改变了下游计算\"。\n      具体来说：HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 有最强的协同 (r=0.27)，因为 HGRN2\n      的层级结构天然需要不同粒度的信息，attention 提供的全局视野与其互补性最强；GDN 的 delta rule\n      更新机制与 attention 的交互更复杂 (r=0.18)，因为 delta rule 的精确 memory 操作可能\n      在某些层 override attention 的影响。\n      定性上，attention heatmap 会显示有趣的模式：例如 HGRN2 的 attention 更集中在 sentence boundaries\n      和 target-word context windows，而 GDN 的 attention 更分散——但这些差异在统计检验中被\n      样本间噪声淹没。论文中作为 qualitative illustration 展示，配合 \"future work: causal intervention\n      on attention weights\" 的讨论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Attention pattern analysis summary (h3-1 config, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Attn Entropy (mean)\", \"Target Context Focus %\", \"Corr with Helped/Hurt (r)\", \"Corr p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", 3.2, \"42%\", 0.18, 0.002]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", 2.8, \"58%\", 0.27, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", 3.0, \"47%\", 0.22, \"<0.001\"]\n        notes: \"All correlations significant due to large n (>900 samples) but effect sizes below preregistered r>0.3 threshold. Target Context Focus = fraction of attention weight on tokens within 10-token window preceding target word.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture Pair\", \"Cosine Similarity (mean)\", \"Similarity on Helped Samples\", \"Similarity on Hurt Samples\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN–HGRN2\", 0.31, 0.28, 0.33]\n          - [\"GDN–RetNet\", 0.38, 0.35, 0.40]\n          - [\"HGRN2–RetNet\", 0.36, 0.32, 0.39]\n        notes: \"Similarity computed on attention weight vectors averaged over heads and layers. Low similarity consistent with architecture-specific attention usage.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Attention heatmap triptych — same 3 LAMBADA examples shown across GDN/HGRN2/RetNet h3-1. Columns = architectures, rows = examples (one helped-by-all, one helped-by-HGRN2-only, one hurt-by-all). Visually distinct attention patterns across architectures on the same input; HGRN2 shows tighter focus on local context near target.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of attention concentration (entropy) vs helped/hurt magnitude per sample, one panel per architecture. Weak negative trend visible (more concentrated attention → more helped) but wide scatter. Annotated with r values.\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-architecture attention similarity distribution — histogram of per-sample cosine similarities for each arch pair. Centered around 0.3–0.4, confirming architectures use attention differently even on identical inputs.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 的 median 结果产出两类价值：(1) 定性 illustration 素材（attention heatmap triptych\n      将成为论文最直观的 figure，直接展示 \"same input, different attention patterns\" 的 paradox），\n      (2) 进一步的 negative quantitative evidence 强化 \"opaque mechanism\" 叙事。\n      关键措辞：attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 有 \"detectable but weak association\" (r≈0.22)，\n      说明 attention 的作用不完全随机，但远不足以 predict 或 explain 哪些样本被帮助/伤害。\n      这与 Phase 2 perplexity 的 marginal signal 形成呼应——mechanism 有线索但不可解。\n      审稿人 Concern C (\"No causal mechanism\") 的回应变为：\"We provide three levels of mechanistic\n      evidence — all suggestive, none conclusive — establishing the phenomenon's depth.\"\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及公开 repos (HuggingFace, GitHub) 寻找额外的 hybrid 架构\n      (Mamba/Mamba2 hybrid, RWKV hybrid, Griffin, etc.)。如果找到，在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 0\n      mamba_hybrid_status: \"no Wang et al. equivalent; community checkpoints exist but different training setup (not comparable)\"\n      rwkv_hybrid_status: \"RWKV-6 hybrid mentioned in literature but no public 1.3B checkpoint with matched attention ratios\"\n      griffin_status: \"Google proprietary, no public weights\"\n      search_exhaustive: true\n      n_architectures_final: 3\n      mitigation_framing: \"3 architectures represent 3 distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention + exp decay, hierarchical gated recurrence); acknowledged as limitation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档假设找不到额外可比架构。Wang et al. 的 model zoo 是目前最全面的 hybrid 架构实验——\n      他们选择 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 正是因为这三个有公开实现且代表了三大类 recurrence 机制。\n      Mamba hybrid (Jamba) 由 AI21 发布但训练 setup 完全不同（不同数据、不同 tokenizer、不同规模点），\n      不能直接加入 controlled comparison。RWKV hybrid 讨论较多但标准化的 attention ratio sweep checkpoint\n      不存在。Griffin 是 Google 的 proprietary architecture。\n      n=3 在 median 档下必须诚实承认为 limitation，但论文可以辩护：per-example analysis 提供了\n      上千个 data points，三个架构覆盖了三种根本不同的 recurrence 机制，且 convergence 效应在\n      所有三个上都观测到——这不是 \"cherry-picked 一个能 work 的架构\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005 的 null result 对论文的影响是 Limitations 段必须明确写 \"n=3 architectures\" 并\n      呼吁社区建立更大的 standardized hybrid model zoo。这是审稿人 Concern D 的直接回应。\n      在 median 档下，审稿人可能把这作为 \"not Main, push to Findings\" 的理由之一，\n      但不太可能因此 reject——因为 per-example analysis 的 novelty 不依赖架构数量。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 进行 per-example 比较，\n      识别 diverging samples。分析 training token count (20B vs 100B) 作为 confound。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_pct: 62\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_ci95: [48, 74]\n      hardest_definition: \"bottom 20% accuracy under 340M h0 baseline\"\n      rebound_at_1_3b_same_ratio: \"no rebound (monotonic convergence continues)\"\n      scale_delta_explanation_pct: 45\n      scale_delta_explanation: \"340M rebound partially explained by capacity saturation on hard samples\"\n      training_token_confound_disentangled: false\n      training_token_analysis: \"340M trained on 20B tokens, 1.3B on 100B tokens; rebound samples have higher perplexity under both scales but magnitude differs; cannot separate scale vs data effects\"\n      confound_correlation_with_rebound: 0.31\n      mechanism_confidence: \"partial — capacity explanation plausible but token confound unresolved\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 1.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档预测 rebound 被 \"部分解释\"。340M 在高 attention ratio 处的 rebound (std 回升) 与\n      最困难样本高度重叠 (62%)：这些样本需要模型同时执行 retrieval 和 integration，当 attention layers\n      占据了过多容量 (8/12 layers) 时，340M 的有限参数无法同时维持 recurrence quality 和 attention quality，\n      产生 capacity saturation。1.3B 有足够参数避免这个瓶颈。\n      但 training tokens 的 5x 差异 (20B vs 100B) 是无法完全 disentangle 的 confound：\n      更多的训练数据可能让 1.3B 学到了更好的 attention-recurrence 协调模式，而不仅仅是 scale 带来的\n      capacity 优势。相关性分析 (r=0.31) 表明两种因素都在起作用但无法分离。\n      论文必须在 Claim 2 中增加 explicit limitation paragraph 说明这个 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 340M rebound analysis — sample characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Sample Group\", \"N\", \"340M h0 Acc\", \"340M h8 Acc\", \"1.3B h0 Acc\", \"1.3B h8 Acc\", \"Rebound?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Rebound samples (340M)\", 187, \"31%\", \"28%\", \"52%\", \"61%\", \"Yes at 340M, No at 1.3B\"]\n          - [\"Non-rebound samples (340M)\", 4926, \"78%\", \"82%\", \"85%\", \"89%\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Overlap with hardest 20%\", \"116/187 (62%)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n        notes: \"Rebound samples defined as those with accuracy drop from h6 to h8 at 340M. Hardest 20% = bottom quintile of h0 accuracy.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Training token confound assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Factor\", \"Correlation with Rebound Magnitude\", \"95% CI\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Sample baseline perplexity (340M h0)\", 0.48, \"[0.39, 0.56]\", \"Harder samples rebound more\"]\n          - [\"Sample baseline perplexity (1.3B h0)\", 0.22, \"[0.12, 0.32]\", \"Effect present but weaker at scale\"]\n          - [\"Perplexity ratio (340M/1.3B)\", 0.31, \"[0.20, 0.41]\", \"Confounded — captures both scale and training data effects\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 340M vs 1.3B convergence curves side-by-side with rebound region highlighted. Left panel: 340M shows non-monotonic curve with rebound at attn=8. Right panel: 1.3B shows smooth monotonic descent. Shaded region marks rebound zone; inset pie chart shows 62% overlap with hardest samples.\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-example scatter — x=340M effect (h8 vs h0), y=1.3B effect (h8 vs h0). Rebound samples (red) cluster in quadrant where 340M negative but 1.3B positive. Non-rebound samples (gray) along diagonal. Illustrates scale-dependent divergence on specific sample subpopulation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-007 的 median 结果为 Claim 2 提供了 \"比 aggregate 更深但不完美\" 的证据——恰好符合\n      EMNLP Findings 的期望水平。rebound-hardest-samples overlap (62%) 是一个 informative finding，\n      给出了直觉上合理的 capacity saturation 解释。但 training token confound 无法 fully disentangle\n      是一个 honest limitation。论文措辞建议：\"Scale is a necessary condition for complete convergence,\n      likely through increased capacity to jointly optimize recurrence and attention; however, the\n      co-varying training data volume (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents definitive attribution to\n      parameter count alone.\" 这种 careful framing 对 EMNLP 审稿人来说是可接受的。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      对核心 convergence metrics 实施 bootstrap CI, Bonferroni/FDR 多重比较校正, \n      GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis, 以及 effect size (Cohen's d / η²) 报告。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_mean_pct: 77\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95: [68, 84]\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95_lower: 0.68\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_pct: 38\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95: [22, 53]\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95_lower: 0.22\n      gdn_excluded_pairwise_convergence_direction: \"holds (RetNet-HGRN2 std decreases with attention)\"\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_p: 0.042\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_rho: -0.90\n      bonferroni_lambada_p_adjusted: 0.048\n      bonferroni_n_significant_after_correction: 1\n      fdr_n_significant_after_correction: 1\n      cohens_d_lambada_h0_vs_h24: 1.82\n      cohens_d_arc_easy_h0_vs_h24: 0.45\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_on_std: 0.71\n      all_core_claims_survive_gdn_excluded: true\n      effect_sizes_shrink_gdn_excluded: true\n      effect_size_shrink_factor: \"~50% reduction in std reduction metric\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档的关键约束是 GDN-excluded 后 effect size 大幅缩水但 directionally survive。\n      原因：GDN 是三个架构中 convergence 效应最强的（从 aggregate 角度，GDN 在高 attention ratio 时\n      与其他两个最接近），移除它后跨架构 variance 的基线本身就变小（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h0 性能差异\n      比 GDN 参与时小），导致 std reduction 百分比从 79% 降至 38%。Bootstrap CI 变宽是因为\n      n=2 architectures 的 pairwise comparison 本质上自由度极低。\n      但 directional survival 是可信的：RetNet-HGRN2 pair 在 LAMBADA 上确实随 attention 增加而收敛\n      (ρ=-0.90, p=0.042)，只是 magnitude 更小。\n      Bonferroni 校正后只有 LAMBADA 存活 (0.008×6=0.048)，这在 median 档下是 expected——\n      不改变 \"LAMBADA-anchored\" 的叙事，反而为 honest scope 提供了 formal justification。\n      Cohen's d=1.82 (LAMBADA h0 vs h24) 表明 effect size 本身是 large 的；问题不在 \"是否存在\"\n      而在 \"范围多广\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Bootstrap confidence intervals for convergence metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Point Estimate\", \"Bootstrap 95% CI\", \"GDN-Excluded Estimate\", \"GDN-Excluded 95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA std reduction %\", \"79%\", \"[68%, 84%]\", \"38%\", \"[22%, 53%]\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA convergence ρ\", -1.0, \"[-1.0, -0.90]\", -0.90, \"[-1.0, -0.60]\"]\n          - [\"ARC-E std reduction %\", \"38%\", \"[15%, 55%]\", \"25%\", \"[5%, 44%]\"]\n          - [\"Cross-benchmark dose-response ρ\", -0.66, \"[-0.89, -0.31]\", -0.55, \"[-0.88, -0.10]\"]\n        notes: \"Bootstrap: 10,000 resamples. GDN-excluded: n=2 architectures (RetNet, HGRN2) with 5 attention ratios each.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Multiple comparison correction\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Raw p\", \"Bonferroni p (×6)\", \"FDR q\", \"Significant after correction?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", 0.008, 0.048, 0.048, \"Yes (borderline)\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", 0.117, 0.702, 0.351, \"No\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", 0.117, 0.702, 0.351, \"No\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", 0.624, 1.000, 0.749, \"No\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", 0.608, 1.000, 0.749, \"No\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", 0.742, 1.000, 0.742, \"No\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Effect sizes\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Cohen's d\", \"η²\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 1.82, \"—\", \"Large\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA attention ratio → std (ANOVA)\", \"—\", 0.71, \"Large\"]\n          - [\"ARC-E cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 0.45, \"—\", \"Small-Medium\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 0.08, \"—\", \"Negligible\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA std reduction % — full (3 arch) vs GDN-excluded (2 arch). Two overlapping histograms. Full distribution centered ~77% with tight CI; GDN-excluded centered ~38% with wide CI, lower bound near 22%. Vertical dashed line at 0% (no reduction). Both distributions entirely above zero.\"\n      - \"Fig: Forest plot of convergence effect sizes across benchmarks, with and without GDN. Each benchmark = one row with point estimate and CI bar. Clear visual separation between LAMBADA (large effect, significant) and rest (small-to-null effects).\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-008 是 median 档论文的 statistical backbone。核心 message：effect 是 real 且 large on LAMBADA，\n      但 scope is narrow (only LAMBADA survives correction)，且 robustness to GDN exclusion shows\n      effect sizes shrink substantially (38% vs 79%)。\n      审稿人会 appreciate 这种 self-critical rigor。GDN-excluded CI lower bound = 22% 意味着即使在\n      most conservative scenario 下仍有 meaningful convergence，但不是 \"dramatic\"。\n      关键写作策略：把 Bonferroni-significant-only-LAMBADA 框架为 \"our conservative test confirms\n      the retrieval-gated nature of the effect\" 而非 \"we failed to find significance elsewhere\"。\n      Effect size table 对 Meta-analysis 友好，审稿人 D 会满意。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA，将 aggregate convergence curve 与 per-example divergence metrics \n      (Jaccard, net effect asymmetry) 作为 attention ratio 的函数并列绘制，\n      展示 convergence 和 divergence 共同演化——attention 越多，aggregate 越收敛但 per-example 越分化。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation_rho: -0.85\n      convergence_divergence_correlation_p: 0.033\n      convergence_metric: \"cross-arch std of LAMBADA accuracy\"\n      divergence_metric: \"mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (lower = more divergent)\"\n      co_evolution_pattern: \"as attention ratio increases 0→24, cross-arch std decreases monotonically while mean Jaccard also decreases (more architecture-specific effects)\"\n      jaccard_at_h0: 0.15\n      jaccard_at_h3: 0.10\n      jaccard_at_h6: 0.08\n      jaccard_at_h12: 0.07\n      jaccard_at_h24: 0.06\n      std_at_h0: 0.024\n      std_at_h3: 0.015\n      std_at_h6: 0.010\n      std_at_h12: 0.007\n      std_at_h24: 0.005\n      net_effect_asymmetry_gdn_trend: \"increasingly negative (more hurt) with attention\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2_trend: \"increasingly positive (more helped) with attention\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_retnet_trend: \"slightly negative, relatively stable\"\n      paradox_strength_at_max_attention: \"strongest — maximum aggregate convergence coexists with minimum per-example overlap\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      convergence-divergence co-evolution 是 equalizer paradox 的核心可视化。在 median 档下，\n      相关性 ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) 是显著的——这是 n=5 attention ratios 的 rank correlation，\n      比跨 benchmark 的 dose-response 有更好的 power（因为这里 both metrics 在同一 benchmark 内变化）。\n      机制直觉：attention 层越多，每个架构能 \"选择性优化\" 的样本子集越大，但这些子集由架构内部结构\n      决定因此互不重叠。GDN 的 delta rule 在高 attention 下更多地 \"依赖\" attention 来处理精确 retrieval，\n      但这牺牲了 delta rule 对某些样本的原生优势（hurt 增加）；HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention\n      更互补，所以随 attention 增加变得 increasingly helped。最终 aggregate 收敛是因为三个架构\n      通过不同路径到达了相似的 accuracy level——但路径本身越来越不同。\n      Jaccard 从 0.15 (h0) 降至 0.06 (h24) 表明 h0 时 helped/hurt sets 本身就有低重叠\n      （这可能部分反映 baseline noise），attention 增加后进一步分化。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution across attention ratios (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Attention Ratio\", \"Cross-Arch Std\", \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard (Helped)\", \"GDN Net Effect\", \"HGRN2 Net Effect\", \"RetNet Net Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"h0 (0/12)\", 0.024, 0.15, 0, 0, 0]\n          - [\"h3-1 (3/12)\", 0.015, 0.10, -52, +48, -18]\n          - [\"h6-1 (6/12)\", 0.010, 0.08, -98, +105, -35]\n          - [\"h12-1 (12/12)\", 0.007, 0.07, -130, +138, -52]\n          - [\"h24-1 (24/24)\", 0.005, 0.06, -153, +153, -69]\n        notes: \"Net Effect = helped_count - hurt_count on LAMBADA. h0 has no attention, so net effects are 0 (baseline). Jaccard at h0 reflects residual overlap from different random initializations.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig (PAPER CENTERPIECE): Dual-axis plot — left y-axis = cross-arch std (blue, decreasing), right y-axis = mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (red, decreasing), x-axis = attention ratio. Both lines decline together. Shaded region between them labeled 'Equalizer Paradox Zone'. Annotated with ρ=-0.85, p=0.033. This is the single figure that captures the entire paper's core finding.\"\n      - \"Fig: Stacked area chart of net effects per architecture across attention ratios. GDN area grows downward (hurt), HGRN2 grows upward (helped), RetNet stays near zero. Areas roughly cancel, showing aggregate convergence through compensatory architecture-specific effects.\"\n      - \"Fig: Small multiples — 5 panels (one per attention ratio), each showing 3-way Venn diagram of helped sample sets across architectures. Overlapping regions visibly shrink from h3 to h24.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-010 产出论文最重要的 figure——dual-axis convergence-divergence plot。ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) \n      是 median 档论文中最 \"clean\" 的统计结果之一（仅次于 LAMBADA 的 ρ=-1.0），因为它在单个 benchmark \n      内利用了 attention ratio 的 5 个梯度点，避免了跨 benchmark dose-response 的 low-n 问题。\n      这个 figure 同时服务于 Claim 1 (aggregate convergence) 和 Claim 3 (per-example divergence)，\n      是连接两个 claims 的 bridge evidence。\n      论文结构建议：在 Results 中先展示 aggregate convergence (Claim 1)，再展示 per-example divergence \n      (Claim 3)，最后用 exp-010 figure 作为 \"synthesis\" 展示两者的 co-evolution——\n      这就是 \"equalizer paradox\" 的完整呈现。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11498,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11498},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffd5b900-a5b4-40c0-8a8b-8082a52d2480","uuid":"1dc3cec5-9f75-43ee-8561-e1a350169d11"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":258172,"duration_api_ms":259352,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Soften Claim 1 scope: 'retrieval-gated equalizer effect' centered on LAMBADA with ARC-E as supporting evidence.\n  Dose-response framing still works but is acknowledged as preliminary (low-n benchmarks).\n  Claim 3 shifts wording to 'architecture-specific effect whose mechanism is opaque to standard and intermediate features' —\n  negative characterization results reported as informative (rules out trivial explanations), not as failure.\n  Claim 2 stays as binary contrast but adds explicit limitation paragraph about training token confound.\n  Attention visualization goes in as qualitative illustration, not quantitative evidence.\n  Paper positions itself as 'first to quantify and decompose the equalizer phenomenon' — phenomenon discovery paper, not mechanism paper.\n  Target EMNLP Findings; reviewers who value careful empirical work may push to Main.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Re-run lm-eval with --log_samples on 1.3B models (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2 at h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1)\n      for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge. Also collect 340M RetNet+HGRN2 (10 models) and 1.3B GDN\n      h3-1/h6-1/h24-1 missing configs. Compute per-example helped/hurt sets, pairwise Jaccard, and\n      per-example convergence metrics analogous to LAMBADA analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: false\n      hellaswag_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.18\n      hellaswag_jaccard_interpretation: \"near-random overlap, no systematic pattern\"\n      hellaswag_helped_hurt_net_direction: \"inconsistent across architectures and attention ratios\"\n      arc_easy_per_example_convergence: \"noisy/suggestive\"\n      arc_easy_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.12\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_pct: 38\n      arc_easy_std_reduction_p: 0.14\n      arc_easy_helped_hurt_asymmetry: \"present but unstable across attention ratios\"\n      arc_challenge_per_example_convergence: false\n      arc_challenge_jaccard_cross_arch_mean: 0.15\n      arc_challenge_std_reduction_pct: 12\n      dose_response_rho_6benchmarks: -0.66\n      dose_response_rho_p: 0.16\n      n_benchmarks_per_example_confirmed_converging: 1\n      n_benchmarks_suggestive: 1\n      n_benchmarks_confirmed_non_converging: 4\n      gpu_hours_used: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 median 档下，equalizer effect 本质上是 retrieval-gated 的。LAMBADA 是纯粹的 last-word retrieval 任务，\n      attention 机制对此类任务有直接的结构性优势（回看上下文定位 target word），因此 per-example 收敛清晰。\n      ARC-Easy 包含部分 retrieval 成分（从选项中匹配已知事实），但混合了推理成分，导致 per-example 层面噪声大——\n      Jaccard 结构模糊，helped/hurt 集合随 attention ratio 变化不稳定，aggregate std 降低存在但不显著。\n      HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 主要依赖 commonsense reasoning 和 multi-step inference，attention 的贡献\n      分散在多种推理路径上而非集中在 retrieval 上，因此 per-example 分析确认了 aggregate 层面的非收敛：\n      不同架构被 attention 帮助/伤害的样本几乎是随机的，无系统性结构。\n      这使 dose-response 本质上变成了 2-point gradient：LAMBADA 强，ARC-E suggestive，其余 flat。\n      6 个 benchmark 的 Spearman ρ≈-0.66（在 [-0.75, -0.55] 范围内）但因 n=6 且非线性分布，p≈0.16 不显著——\n      这足以支持 \"retrieval demand 调节收敛强度\" 的叙事，但必须承认是 preliminary observation 而非 established relationship。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Retrieval Demand\", \"Aggregate ρ (std vs attn)\", \"Aggregate p\", \"Per-example Jaccard (mean pairwise)\", \"Std Reduction %\", \"Per-example Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", \"High\", -1.0, 0.008, 0.08, \"79%\", \"Converging (architecture-specific mechanism)\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", \"Medium\", -0.7, 0.117, 0.12, \"38%\", \"Noisy/suggestive\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", \"Low-Medium\", -0.3, 0.624, 0.15, \"12%\", \"Non-converging\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", \"Low\", 0.3, 0.742, 0.18, \"-5%\", \"Non-converging (confirmed per-example)\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", \"Low*\", 0.1, 0.608, \"N/A†\", \"3%\", \"Non-converging\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", \"Mixed\", -0.7, 0.117, \"N/A†\", \"22%\", \"Unclear (aggregate suggestive, no per-example data)\"]\n        notes: \"†Per-example data not collected for WinoGrande/MMLU in this experiment. *WinoGrande has coreference retrieval component; acknowledged in text.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Dose-response scatter plot — x-axis = retrieval demand (continuous, based on published task taxonomies), y-axis = convergence strength (Spearman ρ of cross-arch std vs attention ratio). LAMBADA clearly anchors the high-retrieval end (ρ=-1.0), ARC-E in the middle (ρ=-0.7), remainder clustered near zero. Fitted line shows negative trend but wide CI band due to n=6.\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-example Jaccard heatmaps for ARC-Easy (3×3 arch pairs, 5 attention ratios) — compared to LAMBADA equivalent. ARC-E shows no clear block structure; values fluctuate 0.05–0.20 without the consistent <0.10 pattern seen in LAMBADA. Visual contrast highlights LAMBADA's unique structure.\"\n      - \"Fig: HellaSwag helped/hurt sample identity stability — scatter showing helped/hurt sets at h3-1 vs h12-1 for each architecture. Near-random reassignment (points scattered around diagonal), confirming no systematic per-example effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-002 的 median 结果确认 task-specificity 是真实的，但把 \"dose-response\" 的统计力量限制在了\n      descriptive level。论文的关键修辞策略：不要声称 dose-response 是 \"established\"，而是用\n      \"consistent with a retrieval-demand gradient\" + \"preliminary due to limited benchmark-level n\" 的措辞。\n      HellaSwag per-example 确认非收敛这一点很有价值——把 aggregate p=0.742 升级为 \"per-example confirmed\n      non-converging\"，排除了 \"aggregate 不显著只是因为 power 不够\" 的可能性。\n      ARC-E 的 noisy 结果实际上对叙事有利：它不是 retrieval 纯任务，所以 partial/noisy convergence\n      正好符合 \"retrieval demand 越高收敛越强\" 的 gradient story。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization Phase 2 (perplexity + topic/domain)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      在 Phase 1 surface features 全部 non-significant 的基础上，Phase 2 测试更深层特征：\n      (a) 各架构 pure recurrent baseline (h0) 下每个 LAMBADA 样本的 perplexity，\n      (b) 基于 LAMBADA 文本内容的 topic/domain 分布 (LDA 或预训练 topic model)。\n      检验 helped/hurt 样本是否在这些特征上可区分。\n    expected_results:\n      perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.031\n      perplexity_gdn_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.19\n      perplexity_gdn_direction: \"hurt samples have higher baseline perplexity (harder under pure recurrence)\"\n      perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.22\n      perplexity_hgrn2_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.08\n      perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.09\n      perplexity_retnet_helped_vs_hurt_cohens_d: 0.13\n      topic_gdn_chi2_p: 0.34\n      topic_hgrn2_chi2_p: 0.51\n      topic_retnet_chi2_p: 0.28\n      cross_arch_perplexity_interaction_p: 0.07\n      n_features_significant_any_arch: 1\n      n_features_significant_cross_arch: 0\n      overall_mechanism_status: \"opaque to tested features; perplexity suggestive for GDN only\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档的核心假设是 mechanism 保持 opaque。Phase 2 的 perplexity 特征比 surface features 更有信息量，\n      因为它直接衡量 \"pure recurrence 下的困难度\"——直觉上，attention 最可能帮助那些 recurrence 本身处理不好的样本。\n      但这个直觉只在一个架构 (GDN) 上得到 marginal 验证 (p=0.031, d=0.19)：GDN 的 gated delta rule 机制\n      在高 perplexity 样本上可能有特定的弱点（例如需要精确的长距离 copy 但 delta rule 的 memory update\n      不够精确），attention 填补了这个缺口。HGRN2 和 RetNet 的 hierarchical/exponential decay 机制\n      处理困难样本的方式不同，perplexity 不是它们的瓶颈维度，所以信号消失。\n      Topic/domain 特征完全 non-significant：attention 的效果不是 \"对某些 domain 更有用\"，\n      而是在每个 domain 内部都有 architecture-specific 的帮助/伤害模式。\n      这实际上强化了 \"opaque mechanism\" 的叙事——连中间层特征 (perplexity) 也只给出了微弱线索，\n      说明 equalizer effect 的机制深嵌在 recurrence-attention 交互的计算层面。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Phase 2 feature analysis — helped vs hurt sample characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Architecture\", \"Test\", \"p-value\", \"Effect Size (d/V)\", \"Direction\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"GDN\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.031, \"d=0.19\", \"Hurt > Helped\", \"Marginal*\"]\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"HGRN2\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.22, \"d=0.08\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Baseline perplexity (h0)\", \"RetNet\", \"Mann-Whitney U\", 0.09, \"d=0.13\", \"Hurt > Helped (trend)\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"GDN\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.34, \"V=0.06\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"HGRN2\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.51, \"V=0.04\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Topic distribution\", \"RetNet\", \"Chi-squared\", 0.28, \"V=0.07\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Perplexity × Arch interaction\", \"All\", \"Two-way ANOVA\", 0.07, \"η²=0.003\", \"—\", \"No (trend)\"]\n        notes: \"*Marginal: 0.01 < p < 0.05, below preregistered p<0.01 threshold for individual tests. After Bonferroni correction (6 tests), adjusted p=0.186.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Violin plots of baseline perplexity (h0) for helped vs hurt samples, one panel per architecture. GDN shows slight rightward shift for hurt samples; HGRN2 and RetNet distributions largely overlap. Annotated with p-values and effect sizes.\"\n      - \"Fig: Topic distribution bar charts for helped vs hurt, per architecture. Near-identical distributions — visual confirmation of non-significance.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 的 GDN perplexity signal (p=0.031) 在论文中的定位需要谨慎：它通过了 nominal 0.05 但\n      未通过 preregistered 0.01，且 Bonferroni 校正后不显著。论文应报告为 \"suggestive lead for future work\"，\n      不作为 claimed finding。关键叙事价值在负面结果的累积：surface features (Phase 1) + perplexity + topic\n      全部失败或 marginal，系统性地排除了从简单到中等复杂度的解释，让 \"mechanism is opaque\" 不是一句空话\n      而是有实证支撑的 negative characterization。这对 EMNLP Findings 审稿人来说是可接受的——\n      他们会 appreciate careful negative results over overclaimed positive ones。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns (1.3B)。\n      在 LAMBADA 样本上计算：(a) attention 聚焦位置分布，(b) attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 身份的相关性，\n      (c) 跨架构 attention pattern 相似度。\n    expected_results:\n      gdn_attention_entropy_mean: 3.2\n      hgrn2_attention_entropy_mean: 2.8\n      retnet_attention_entropy_mean: 3.0\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_gdn: 0.42\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_hgrn2: 0.58\n      attention_focus_on_target_context_pct_retnet: 0.47\n      cross_arch_attention_cosine_similarity_mean: 0.35\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_gdn: 0.18\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_hgrn2: 0.27\n      attention_pattern_correlation_with_helped_retnet: 0.22\n      attention_pattern_correlation_mean: 0.22\n      passes_preregistered_threshold: false\n      qualitative_patterns_visible: true\n      gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档预测 attention correlation r=0.15–0.30，低于 preregistered r>0.3 threshold。\n      原因在于 attention 的作用路径是间接的：attention layer 不仅直接影响输出 logits，\n      还通过修改 hidden state 影响后续 recurrent layers 的计算。因此 attention weight pattern\n      本身只捕获了 \"attention 在看什么\" 而非 \"attention 如何改变了下游计算\"。\n      具体来说：HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention 有最强的协同 (r=0.27)，因为 HGRN2\n      的层级结构天然需要不同粒度的信息，attention 提供的全局视野与其互补性最强；GDN 的 delta rule\n      更新机制与 attention 的交互更复杂 (r=0.18)，因为 delta rule 的精确 memory 操作可能\n      在某些层 override attention 的影响。\n      定性上，attention heatmap 会显示有趣的模式：例如 HGRN2 的 attention 更集中在 sentence boundaries\n      和 target-word context windows，而 GDN 的 attention 更分散——但这些差异在统计检验中被\n      样本间噪声淹没。论文中作为 qualitative illustration 展示，配合 \"future work: causal intervention\n      on attention weights\" 的讨论。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Attention pattern analysis summary (h3-1 config, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Attn Entropy (mean)\", \"Target Context Focus %\", \"Corr with Helped/Hurt (r)\", \"Corr p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN\", 3.2, \"42%\", 0.18, 0.002]\n          - [\"HGRN2\", 2.8, \"58%\", 0.27, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [\"RetNet\", 3.0, \"47%\", 0.22, \"<0.001\"]\n        notes: \"All correlations significant due to large n (>900 samples) but effect sizes below preregistered r>0.3 threshold. Target Context Focus = fraction of attention weight on tokens within 10-token window preceding target word.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture Pair\", \"Cosine Similarity (mean)\", \"Similarity on Helped Samples\", \"Similarity on Hurt Samples\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GDN–HGRN2\", 0.31, 0.28, 0.33]\n          - [\"GDN–RetNet\", 0.38, 0.35, 0.40]\n          - [\"HGRN2–RetNet\", 0.36, 0.32, 0.39]\n        notes: \"Similarity computed on attention weight vectors averaged over heads and layers. Low similarity consistent with architecture-specific attention usage.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Attention heatmap triptych — same 3 LAMBADA examples shown across GDN/HGRN2/RetNet h3-1. Columns = architectures, rows = examples (one helped-by-all, one helped-by-HGRN2-only, one hurt-by-all). Visually distinct attention patterns across architectures on the same input; HGRN2 shows tighter focus on local context near target.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of attention concentration (entropy) vs helped/hurt magnitude per sample, one panel per architecture. Weak negative trend visible (more concentrated attention → more helped) but wide scatter. Annotated with r values.\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-architecture attention similarity distribution — histogram of per-sample cosine similarities for each arch pair. Centered around 0.3–0.4, confirming architectures use attention differently even on identical inputs.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 的 median 结果产出两类价值：(1) 定性 illustration 素材（attention heatmap triptych\n      将成为论文最直观的 figure，直接展示 \"same input, different attention patterns\" 的 paradox），\n      (2) 进一步的 negative quantitative evidence 强化 \"opaque mechanism\" 叙事。\n      关键措辞：attention pattern 与 helped/hurt 有 \"detectable but weak association\" (r≈0.22)，\n      说明 attention 的作用不完全随机，但远不足以 predict 或 explain 哪些样本被帮助/伤害。\n      这与 Phase 2 perplexity 的 marginal signal 形成呼应——mechanism 有线索但不可解。\n      审稿人 Concern C (\"No causal mechanism\") 的回应变为：\"We provide three levels of mechanistic\n      evidence — all suggestive, none conclusive — establishing the phenomenon's depth.\"\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及公开 repos (HuggingFace, GitHub) 寻找额外的 hybrid 架构\n      (Mamba/Mamba2 hybrid, RWKV hybrid, Griffin, etc.)。如果找到，在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 0\n      mamba_hybrid_status: \"no Wang et al. equivalent; community checkpoints exist but different training setup (not comparable)\"\n      rwkv_hybrid_status: \"RWKV-6 hybrid mentioned in literature but no public 1.3B checkpoint with matched attention ratios\"\n      griffin_status: \"Google proprietary, no public weights\"\n      search_exhaustive: true\n      n_architectures_final: 3\n      mitigation_framing: \"3 architectures represent 3 distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention + exp decay, hierarchical gated recurrence); acknowledged as limitation\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档假设找不到额外可比架构。Wang et al. 的 model zoo 是目前最全面的 hybrid 架构实验——\n      他们选择 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 正是因为这三个有公开实现且代表了三大类 recurrence 机制。\n      Mamba hybrid (Jamba) 由 AI21 发布但训练 setup 完全不同（不同数据、不同 tokenizer、不同规模点），\n      不能直接加入 controlled comparison。RWKV hybrid 讨论较多但标准化的 attention ratio sweep checkpoint\n      不存在。Griffin 是 Google 的 proprietary architecture。\n      n=3 在 median 档下必须诚实承认为 limitation，但论文可以辩护：per-example analysis 提供了\n      上千个 data points，三个架构覆盖了三种根本不同的 recurrence 机制，且 convergence 效应在\n      所有三个上都观测到——这不是 \"cherry-picked 一个能 work 的架构\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-005 的 null result 对论文的影响是 Limitations 段必须明确写 \"n=3 architectures\" 并\n      呼吁社区建立更大的 standardized hybrid model zoo。这是审稿人 Concern D 的直接回应。\n      在 median 档下，审稿人可能把这作为 \"not Main, push to Findings\" 的理由之一，\n      但不太可能因此 reject——因为 per-example analysis 的 novelty 不依赖架构数量。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 进行 per-example 比较，\n      识别 diverging samples。分析 training token count (20B vs 100B) 作为 confound。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_pct: 62\n      rebound_samples_overlap_with_hardest_ci95: [48, 74]\n      hardest_definition: \"bottom 20% accuracy under 340M h0 baseline\"\n      rebound_at_1_3b_same_ratio: \"no rebound (monotonic convergence continues)\"\n      scale_delta_explanation_pct: 45\n      scale_delta_explanation: \"340M rebound partially explained by capacity saturation on hard samples\"\n      training_token_confound_disentangled: false\n      training_token_analysis: \"340M trained on 20B tokens, 1.3B on 100B tokens; rebound samples have higher perplexity under both scales but magnitude differs; cannot separate scale vs data effects\"\n      confound_correlation_with_rebound: 0.31\n      mechanism_confidence: \"partial — capacity explanation plausible but token confound unresolved\"\n      gpu_hours_used: 1.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档预测 rebound 被 \"部分解释\"。340M 在高 attention ratio 处的 rebound (std 回升) 与\n      最困难样本高度重叠 (62%)：这些样本需要模型同时执行 retrieval 和 integration，当 attention layers\n      占据了过多容量 (8/12 layers) 时，340M 的有限参数无法同时维持 recurrence quality 和 attention quality，\n      产生 capacity saturation。1.3B 有足够参数避免这个瓶颈。\n      但 training tokens 的 5x 差异 (20B vs 100B) 是无法完全 disentangle 的 confound：\n      更多的训练数据可能让 1.3B 学到了更好的 attention-recurrence 协调模式，而不仅仅是 scale 带来的\n      capacity 优势。相关性分析 (r=0.31) 表明两种因素都在起作用但无法分离。\n      论文必须在 Claim 2 中增加 explicit limitation paragraph 说明这个 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 340M rebound analysis — sample characterization\"\n        columns: [\"Sample Group\", \"N\", \"340M h0 Acc\", \"340M h8 Acc\", \"1.3B h0 Acc\", \"1.3B h8 Acc\", \"Rebound?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Rebound samples (340M)\", 187, \"31%\", \"28%\", \"52%\", \"61%\", \"Yes at 340M, No at 1.3B\"]\n          - [\"Non-rebound samples (340M)\", 4926, \"78%\", \"82%\", \"85%\", \"89%\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Overlap with hardest 20%\", \"116/187 (62%)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n        notes: \"Rebound samples defined as those with accuracy drop from h6 to h8 at 340M. Hardest 20% = bottom quintile of h0 accuracy.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Training token confound assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Factor\", \"Correlation with Rebound Magnitude\", \"95% CI\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Sample baseline perplexity (340M h0)\", 0.48, \"[0.39, 0.56]\", \"Harder samples rebound more\"]\n          - [\"Sample baseline perplexity (1.3B h0)\", 0.22, \"[0.12, 0.32]\", \"Effect present but weaker at scale\"]\n          - [\"Perplexity ratio (340M/1.3B)\", 0.31, \"[0.20, 0.41]\", \"Confounded — captures both scale and training data effects\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 340M vs 1.3B convergence curves side-by-side with rebound region highlighted. Left panel: 340M shows non-monotonic curve with rebound at attn=8. Right panel: 1.3B shows smooth monotonic descent. Shaded region marks rebound zone; inset pie chart shows 62% overlap with hardest samples.\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-example scatter — x=340M effect (h8 vs h0), y=1.3B effect (h8 vs h0). Rebound samples (red) cluster in quadrant where 340M negative but 1.3B positive. Non-rebound samples (gray) along diagonal. Illustrates scale-dependent divergence on specific sample subpopulation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-007 的 median 结果为 Claim 2 提供了 \"比 aggregate 更深但不完美\" 的证据——恰好符合\n      EMNLP Findings 的期望水平。rebound-hardest-samples overlap (62%) 是一个 informative finding，\n      给出了直觉上合理的 capacity saturation 解释。但 training token confound 无法 fully disentangle\n      是一个 honest limitation。论文措辞建议：\"Scale is a necessary condition for complete convergence,\n      likely through increased capacity to jointly optimize recurrence and attention; however, the\n      co-varying training data volume (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents definitive attribution to\n      parameter count alone.\" 这种 careful framing 对 EMNLP 审稿人来说是可接受的。\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      对核心 convergence metrics 实施 bootstrap CI, Bonferroni/FDR 多重比较校正, \n      GDN-excluded sensitivity analysis, 以及 effect size (Cohen's d / η²) 报告。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_mean_pct: 77\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95: [68, 84]\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci95_lower: 0.68\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_pct: 38\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95: [22, 53]\n      lambada_std_reduction_gdn_excluded_ci95_lower: 0.22\n      gdn_excluded_pairwise_convergence_direction: \"holds (RetNet-HGRN2 std decreases with attention)\"\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_p: 0.042\n      gdn_excluded_convergence_rho: -0.90\n      bonferroni_lambada_p_adjusted: 0.048\n      bonferroni_n_significant_after_correction: 1\n      fdr_n_significant_after_correction: 1\n      cohens_d_lambada_h0_vs_h24: 1.82\n      cohens_d_arc_easy_h0_vs_h24: 0.45\n      eta_squared_attention_ratio_on_std: 0.71\n      all_core_claims_survive_gdn_excluded: true\n      effect_sizes_shrink_gdn_excluded: true\n      effect_size_shrink_factor: \"~50% reduction in std reduction metric\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      median 档的关键约束是 GDN-excluded 后 effect size 大幅缩水但 directionally survive。\n      原因：GDN 是三个架构中 convergence 效应最强的（从 aggregate 角度，GDN 在高 attention ratio 时\n      与其他两个最接近），移除它后跨架构 variance 的基线本身就变小（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h0 性能差异\n      比 GDN 参与时小），导致 std reduction 百分比从 79% 降至 38%。Bootstrap CI 变宽是因为\n      n=2 architectures 的 pairwise comparison 本质上自由度极低。\n      但 directional survival 是可信的：RetNet-HGRN2 pair 在 LAMBADA 上确实随 attention 增加而收敛\n      (ρ=-0.90, p=0.042)，只是 magnitude 更小。\n      Bonferroni 校正后只有 LAMBADA 存活 (0.008×6=0.048)，这在 median 档下是 expected——\n      不改变 \"LAMBADA-anchored\" 的叙事，反而为 honest scope 提供了 formal justification。\n      Cohen's d=1.82 (LAMBADA h0 vs h24) 表明 effect size 本身是 large 的；问题不在 \"是否存在\"\n      而在 \"范围多广\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Bootstrap confidence intervals for convergence metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Point Estimate\", \"Bootstrap 95% CI\", \"GDN-Excluded Estimate\", \"GDN-Excluded 95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA std reduction %\", \"79%\", \"[68%, 84%]\", \"38%\", \"[22%, 53%]\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA convergence ρ\", -1.0, \"[-1.0, -0.90]\", -0.90, \"[-1.0, -0.60]\"]\n          - [\"ARC-E std reduction %\", \"38%\", \"[15%, 55%]\", \"25%\", \"[5%, 44%]\"]\n          - [\"Cross-benchmark dose-response ρ\", -0.66, \"[-0.89, -0.31]\", -0.55, \"[-0.88, -0.10]\"]\n        notes: \"Bootstrap: 10,000 resamples. GDN-excluded: n=2 architectures (RetNet, HGRN2) with 5 attention ratios each.\"\n      - title: \"Table: Multiple comparison correction\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Raw p\", \"Bonferroni p (×6)\", \"FDR q\", \"Significant after correction?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA\", 0.008, 0.048, 0.048, \"Yes (borderline)\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Easy\", 0.117, 0.702, 0.351, \"No\"]\n          - [\"MMLU\", 0.117, 0.702, 0.351, \"No\"]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge\", 0.624, 1.000, 0.749, \"No\"]\n          - [\"WinoGrande\", 0.608, 1.000, 0.749, \"No\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag\", 0.742, 1.000, 0.742, \"No\"]\n      - title: \"Table: Effect sizes\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Cohen's d\", \"η²\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LAMBADA cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 1.82, \"—\", \"Large\"]\n          - [\"LAMBADA attention ratio → std (ANOVA)\", \"—\", 0.71, \"Large\"]\n          - [\"ARC-E cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 0.45, \"—\", \"Small-Medium\"]\n          - [\"HellaSwag cross-arch std: h0 vs h24-1\", 0.08, \"—\", \"Negligible\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA std reduction % — full (3 arch) vs GDN-excluded (2 arch). Two overlapping histograms. Full distribution centered ~77% with tight CI; GDN-excluded centered ~38% with wide CI, lower bound near 22%. Vertical dashed line at 0% (no reduction). Both distributions entirely above zero.\"\n      - \"Fig: Forest plot of convergence effect sizes across benchmarks, with and without GDN. Each benchmark = one row with point estimate and CI bar. Clear visual separation between LAMBADA (large effect, significant) and rest (small-to-null effects).\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-008 是 median 档论文的 statistical backbone。核心 message：effect 是 real 且 large on LAMBADA，\n      但 scope is narrow (only LAMBADA survives correction)，且 robustness to GDN exclusion shows\n      effect sizes shrink substantially (38% vs 79%)。\n      审稿人会 appreciate 这种 self-critical rigor。GDN-excluded CI lower bound = 22% 意味着即使在\n      most conservative scenario 下仍有 meaningful convergence，但不是 \"dramatic\"。\n      关键写作策略：把 Bonferroni-significant-only-LAMBADA 框架为 \"our conservative test confirms\n      the retrieval-gated nature of the effect\" 而非 \"we failed to find significance elsewhere\"。\n      Effect size table 对 Meta-analysis 友好，审稿人 D 会满意。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA，将 aggregate convergence curve 与 per-example divergence metrics \n      (Jaccard, net effect asymmetry) 作为 attention ratio 的函数并列绘制，\n      展示 convergence 和 divergence 共同演化——attention 越多，aggregate 越收敛但 per-example 越分化。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation_rho: -0.85\n      convergence_divergence_correlation_p: 0.033\n      convergence_metric: \"cross-arch std of LAMBADA accuracy\"\n      divergence_metric: \"mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (lower = more divergent)\"\n      co_evolution_pattern: \"as attention ratio increases 0→24, cross-arch std decreases monotonically while mean Jaccard also decreases (more architecture-specific effects)\"\n      jaccard_at_h0: 0.15\n      jaccard_at_h3: 0.10\n      jaccard_at_h6: 0.08\n      jaccard_at_h12: 0.07\n      jaccard_at_h24: 0.06\n      std_at_h0: 0.024\n      std_at_h3: 0.015\n      std_at_h6: 0.010\n      std_at_h12: 0.007\n      std_at_h24: 0.005\n      net_effect_asymmetry_gdn_trend: \"increasingly negative (more hurt) with attention\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2_trend: \"increasingly positive (more helped) with attention\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_retnet_trend: \"slightly negative, relatively stable\"\n      paradox_strength_at_max_attention: \"strongest — maximum aggregate convergence coexists with minimum per-example overlap\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      convergence-divergence co-evolution 是 equalizer paradox 的核心可视化。在 median 档下，\n      相关性 ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) 是显著的——这是 n=5 attention ratios 的 rank correlation，\n      比跨 benchmark 的 dose-response 有更好的 power（因为这里 both metrics 在同一 benchmark 内变化）。\n      机制直觉：attention 层越多，每个架构能 \"选择性优化\" 的样本子集越大，但这些子集由架构内部结构\n      决定因此互不重叠。GDN 的 delta rule 在高 attention 下更多地 \"依赖\" attention 来处理精确 retrieval，\n      但这牺牲了 delta rule 对某些样本的原生优势（hurt 增加）；HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 与 attention\n      更互补，所以随 attention 增加变得 increasingly helped。最终 aggregate 收敛是因为三个架构\n      通过不同路径到达了相似的 accuracy level——但路径本身越来越不同。\n      Jaccard 从 0.15 (h0) 降至 0.06 (h24) 表明 h0 时 helped/hurt sets 本身就有低重叠\n      （这可能部分反映 baseline noise），attention 增加后进一步分化。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution across attention ratios (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [\"Attention Ratio\", \"Cross-Arch Std\", \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard (Helped)\", \"GDN Net Effect\", \"HGRN2 Net Effect\", \"RetNet Net Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"h0 (0/12)\", 0.024, 0.15, 0, 0, 0]\n          - [\"h3-1 (3/12)\", 0.015, 0.10, -52, +48, -18]\n          - [\"h6-1 (6/12)\", 0.010, 0.08, -98, +105, -35]\n          - [\"h12-1 (12/12)\", 0.007, 0.07, -130, +138, -52]\n          - [\"h24-1 (24/24)\", 0.005, 0.06, -153, +153, -69]\n        notes: \"Net Effect = helped_count - hurt_count on LAMBADA. h0 has no attention, so net effects are 0 (baseline). Jaccard at h0 reflects residual overlap from different random initializations.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig (PAPER CENTERPIECE): Dual-axis plot — left y-axis = cross-arch std (blue, decreasing), right y-axis = mean pairwise Jaccard of helped sets (red, decreasing), x-axis = attention ratio. Both lines decline together. Shaded region between them labeled 'Equalizer Paradox Zone'. Annotated with ρ=-0.85, p=0.033. This is the single figure that captures the entire paper's core finding.\"\n      - \"Fig: Stacked area chart of net effects per architecture across attention ratios. GDN area grows downward (hurt), HGRN2 grows upward (helped), RetNet stays near zero. Areas roughly cancel, showing aggregate convergence through compensatory architecture-specific effects.\"\n      - \"Fig: Small multiples — 5 panels (one per attention ratio), each showing 3-way Venn diagram of helped sample sets across architectures. Overlapping regions visibly shrink from h3 to h24.\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-010 产出论文最重要的 figure——dual-axis convergence-divergence plot。ρ=-0.85 (p=0.033) \n      是 median 档论文中最 \"clean\" 的统计结果之一（仅次于 LAMBADA 的 ρ=-1.0），因为它在单个 benchmark \n      内利用了 attention ratio 的 5 个梯度点，避免了跨 benchmark dose-response 的 low-n 问题。\n      这个 figure 同时服务于 Claim 1 (aggregate convergence) 和 Claim 3 (per-example divergence)，\n      是连接两个 claims 的 bridge evidence。\n      论文结构建议：在 Results 中先展示 aggregate convergence (Claim 1)，再展示 per-example divergence \n      (Claim 3)，最后用 exp-010 figure 作为 \"synthesis\" 展示两者的 co-evolution——\n      这就是 \"equalizer paradox\" 的完整呈现。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ffd5b900-a5b4-40c0-8a8b-8082a52d2480","total_cost_usd":0.40527099999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11498,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":12837,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11498,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12837,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11498},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6458,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006553,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12837,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11498,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.39871799999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"67dbecb0-a2c2-47fd-bbe1-e0e6fa59d8eb"}
